{'question': 'The pain on the right side of my face started about one month ago. At first, it came in attacks that lasted minutes to hours, with periods of relief in between — sometimes up to several hours. But over time, the pain became constant and severe, with no real pain-free periods anymore.

The pain is sharp and stabbing — especially when I clench my jaw or chew, which makes it worse immediately. It starts on the inner part of my nose and radiates across my cheek and upper gum toward my ear. I also noticed some eye tearing and redness at one point, but that’s not happening now.

I don’t feel like there are specific triggers that make it worse — although jaw movement definitely makes it worse right away. I’ve tried putting a towel over my right side of the face, and that helps a little bit.'}
